            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"quotes\": [\n        \"a covered entity must obtain an authorization for any use or disclosure of protected health information for marketing\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposal accurately captures the core requirement under 45 CFR § 164.508(a)(3)(i) mandating that a covered entity obtain an authorization for marketing uses and disclosures of protected health information, correctly incorporating the subpart scope and transition carve-out. It addresses missing inventory unit U0001.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"quotes\": [\n        \"A face-to-face communication made by a covered entity to an individual\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposal correctly identifies and extracts the statutory exception under 45 CFR § 164.508(a)(3)(i)(A) for face-to-face marketing communications made by a covered entity to an individual. It satisfies missing inventory unit U0002.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0002\",\n      \"quotes\": [\n        \"A promotional gift of nominal value provided by the covered entity.\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposal faithfully captures the exception under 45 CFR § 164.508(a)(3)(i)(B) exempting promotional gifts of nominal value provided by a covered entity from the marketing authorization mandate. It satisfies missing inventory unit U0003.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0003\",\n      \"quotes\": [\n        \"the authorization must state that such remuneration is involved.\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposal accurately recovers the mandate in 45 CFR § 164.508(a)(3)(ii) requiring the authorization to state that financial remuneration is involved when marketing involves third-party remuneration as defined in § 164.501. It satisfies missing inventory unit U0006.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
